From 90e3be044ebc84a926e1f57433662b08c8844f0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:06:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui): a refused generation shows the moves it had built
 as a ghost

#261 part 3. A refusal raised with a path in hand now carries that path
as a display-only diagnostic ghost, on the carrier part 2 built for the
refusal's spot: GenError::Ghosted -> CommandError::MachiningGhost ->
State::feedback_ghost. The viewport draws it dashed in the dimmed gouge
colour, without chevrons, and it retires with the refusal sentence. It
is never cached on the operation: the op still has no toolpath, the post
refuses it as ungenerated and the simulation has nothing to play.

Adopters: the ladders' centre-cutting refusal (pocket/adaptive/offset,
contour, contour chain, slot, bore, circular, the 3-D ladder) and the
plunge law's audit of a finished path (finish and multiaxis guards,
Rotary Offset's bar audit, the posed audit, the facer's air entry).
Rotary Offset's wrap-space ladder drops its ghost. Capped at 100k moves;
non-finite ghosts are dropped. The script/MCP generate error names the
ghost's move count.

Fixes #261

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
